# MadGraph5 batch script: ta+ ta- > t t~ NP<=1
# in SMEFTsim_topU3l_MwScheme (UFO v3.0.2), restricted by restrict_vg_cleQt3.dat.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   The tensor-tensor four-fermion operator O_leQt3. Its Lorentz structure is a
#   product of four `Gamma` factors whose index graph is a 4-cycle: no rooting of
#   a tree can evaluate it, which makes this the one row that cannot be reached
#   without a rank-2 tensor intermediate.
#
#   Taus rather than electrons, and a card that restores the tau mass and Yukawa,
#   because the topU3l flavour assumption puts a lepton Yukawa spurion on every
#   chirality-flipping lepton operator: with the shipped massless-lepton values
#   every cyclic-tensor vertex in the model vanishes and MadGraph reports `NP`
#   itself as an unknown coupling order. The tau is the lepton whose restored
#   Yukawa perturbs the rest of the model least.
#
# The model path is repo-relative to the vendored UFO; build.sh rewrites it to
# the work-area copy it stages under output/models/, which is where the
# vg_* restrict cards of validation/madgraph/cards/smeft/ are placed. Both
# generators therefore prune vertices from the same card.
#
# `display interactions` prints the count MadGraph's own interaction splitting
# arrives at (one interaction per coupling-order tuple, import_ufo.add_interaction)
# into the build log, which is where extract_interactions.py reads it from.
#
# Orders are explicit because SMEFTsim gives NP hierarchy 99: MadGraph's default
# WEIGHTED bound would drop every diagram carrying a Wilson coefficient.
import model validation/ufo/SMEFTsim_topU3l_MwScheme_UFO-vg_cleQt3
display interactions
generate ta+ ta- > t t~ NP<=1
output tata_to_ttx_tensor4f -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
